### User Service - example requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Start: docker compose (mysql) -> eureka-server -> user-service
### Direct calls on port 8092 (through the gateway: http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users).
### Run the requests IN ORDER: the POSTs store the new ids for the later requests.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8092
@users = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users

### 0. Health - expect "status":"UP" with "db" UP
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### ===================== CREATE 10 USERS =====================
### Each expects 201 Created, "status": "ACTIVE", "version": 0 and a Location header.

### 1. Aarav Sharma
POST {{users}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "aarav.sharma@example.com",
  "firstName": "Aarav",
  "lastName": "Sharma",
  "phoneNumber": "+919876543210"
}

//> {% client.global.set("user1", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Priya Nair
POST {{users}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya.nair@example.com",
  "firstName": "Priya",
  "lastName": "Nair",
  "phoneNumber": "+919812345678"
}

//> {% client.global.set("user2", response.body.id); %}

