### ===================== READ & SEARCH =====================

### 11. Get one user
//GET {{users}}/{{user1}}

### 12. List all - newest first, expect "totalElements": 10
GET {{users}}

### 13. Sort by last name A-Z, 5 per page
GET {{users}}?sortBy=last_name&size=5

### 14. Next page
GET {{users}}?sortBy=last_name&size=5&page=1

### 15. Text search in names and email - expect Aarav Sharma
GET {{users}}?q=sharma

### 16. Exact email (case-insensitive) - expect Rahul Verma
GET {{users}}?email=RAHUL.VERMA@example.com

### ===================== UPDATE (optimistic locking) =====================

### 17. Update with the CURRENT version 0 - expect 200 and "version": 1
//PUT {{users}}/{{user2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 0,
  "email": "priya.nair@example.com",
  "firstName": "Priya",
  "lastName": "Nair-Menon",
  "phoneNumber": "+919812345679"
}

### 18. Update with an OLD version (0) - expect 409 "Stale version"
//PUT {{users}}/{{user2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 0,
  "email": "priya.nair@example.com",
  "firstName": "Lost",
  "lastName": "Update"
}

### 19. Change email to one that another user has - expect 409 "Duplicate email"
//PUT {{users}}/{{user3}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 0,
  "email": "aarav.sharma@example.com",
  "firstName": "Rahul",
  "lastName": "Verma"
}

### ===================== STATUS LIFE CYCLE =====================

### 20. Suspend - expect "status": "SUSPENDED", "version": 1
//PUT {{users}}/{{user7}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "SUSPENDED",
  "version": 0
}

### 21. Only suspended users - expect David Thompson
GET {{users}}?status=suspended

### 22. Re-activate - expect "status": "ACTIVE", "version": 2
//PUT {{users}}/{{user7}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "version": 1
}

### 23. Try to delete through the status endpoint - expect 409 (use DELETE instead)
//PUT {{users}}/{{user7}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "DELETED",
  "version": 2
}

### ===================== SOFT DELETE =====================

### 24. Delete - expect 204
//DELETE {{users}}/{{user10}}

### 25. Deleted user is still readable - expect "status": "DELETED" and a "deletedAt" timestamp
//GET {{users}}/{{user10}}

### 26. Hidden from the normal list - expect "totalElements": 9
GET {{users}}

### 27. Only deleted users - expect Sofía Rodríguez-López
GET {{users}}?status=deleted

### 28. Update a deleted user - expect 409 "Operation not allowed"
//PUT {{users}}/{{user10}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1,
  "email": "sofia.rodriguez@example.com",
  "firstName": "Sofía",
  "lastName": "Rodríguez"
}

### 29. Delete again - expect 204 (idempotent)
//DELETE {{users}}/{{user10}}

### ===================== VALIDATION & ERRORS =====================

### 30. Duplicate email (different case) - expect 409 "Duplicate email"
POST {{users}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "Aarav.Sharma@EXAMPLE.com",
  "firstName": "Another",
  "lastName": "Aarav"
}

### 31. Invalid body - expect 400 with errors for email, firstName, lastName and phoneNumber
POST {{users}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "Smith123",
  "phoneNumber": "98765"
}

### 32. Unknown id - expect 404 "User not found"
GET {{users}}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 33. Invalid id format - expect 400
GET {{users}}/not-a-uuid

### 34. Invalid page size - expect 400, "errors": {"size": "size must be at most 100"}
GET {{users}}?size=500
